From 009681361ff0c442ea2e79a7b52fa086640cacb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manish Poduval <manupodu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:09:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Web: tutorial bridge (postMessage control channel) and
 ui.landmarks

A page that embeds the web build in an iframe can drive and read the editor
through postMessage: the control channel's engine.execute, document.inspect,
node.get, ui.inspect, ui.set and the new ui.landmarks, for pages on allowed
origins only, with sharing, plugins, saving, exporting and links refused.

ui.landmarks reports named interface rectangles (toolbar groups, panels,
layer rows, the auto layout section's controls) and layers' screen boxes,
so a tutorial can point at a control.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
